" 1849 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{14}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/state.json" "file_sha256" "09dde97fbd5912e561fd4e68e4e2e87eeb966de476d17333b3611bd502e1f6af" "basis" 1849 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-97417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/state.json" "file_sha256" "09dde97fbd5912e561fd4e68e4e2e87eeb966de476d17333b3611bd502e1f6af" "basis" 1849 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNormalize the vector $f(t)=t-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/state.json" "file_sha256" "09dde97fbd5912e561fd4e68e4e2e87eeb966de476d17333b3611bd502e1f6af" "basis" 1849 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{(t-1)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,({t}^{2}-2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-{t}^{2}+t)|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-1+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $f(t),$ we divide $f(t)$ by its norm $‖f(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\frac{f(t)}{‖f(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{t-1}{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(t-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/state.json" "file_sha256" "09dde97fbd5912e561fd4e68e4e2e87eeb966de476d17333b3611bd502e1f6af" "basis" 1849 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "80fec36a7cafbb2fd5ad8479fee505def4c237401c1797d0842fb782d46a9cee" "basis" 1849 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/state.json" "file_sha256" "09dde97fbd5912e561fd4e68e4e2e87eeb966de476d17333b3611bd502e1f6af" "basis" 1849 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-42739" "f