 "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/state.json" "file_sha256" "09dde97fbd5912e561fd4e68e4e2e87eeb966de476d17333b3611bd502e1f6af" "basis" 1849 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057327/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-42739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNormalize the vector $f(t)=t-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-42739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{(t-1)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,({t}^{2}-2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-{t}^{2}+t)|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-1+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $f(t),$ we divide $f(t)$ by its norm $‖f(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\frac{f(t)}{‖f(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{t-1}{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(t-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-42739" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec2c08eedc1aaaa54e0e9cb11c912949cecd1e2a72662dd7171720e0a72d9899"} {"question" "q-42739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-42739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4(t-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}(t-1)"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}(t-1)"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}(t-1)"] ["math" "t-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-42739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{3}(t-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-42763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V=C[0,2]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,2],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=t+{t}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-42763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(t+{t}^{2})^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}+{t}^{4})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}+\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}+8+\\frac{32}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{256}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{\\frac{256}{15}}=\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{15}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-42763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec2c08eedc1aaaa54e0e9cb11c912949cecd1e2a72662dd7171720e0a72d9899"} {"question" "q-42763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-42763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{16}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{15}}"] ["math" "\\frac{256}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-42763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{15}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-97417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(0)y(0)+x(-1)y(-1).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=2t-{t}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-97417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=2t-{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=1,\\,p(0)=0,\\,p(-1)=-3.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(0)p(0)+p(-1)p(-1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(0)]^{2}+[p(-1)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+0+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-97417" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec2c08eedc1aaaa54e0e9cb11c912949cecd1e2a72662dd7171720e0a72d9899"} {"question" "q-97417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-97417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\sqrt{10}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{14}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-97417" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{10}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-97426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(-2)y(-2)+x(0)y(0)+x(2)y(2).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=3-t+{t}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-97426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=3-t+{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(-2)=9,\\,p(0)=3,\\,p(2)=5.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(-2)p(-2)+p(0)p(0)+p(2)p(2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(-2)]^{2}+[p(0)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(9)^{2}+(3)^{2}+(5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81+9+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{115}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-97426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ec2c08eedc1aaaa54e0e9cb11c912949cecd1e2a72662dd7171720e0a72d9899"} {"question" "q-97426" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-97426" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{105}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{115}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067598/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb70cae732b893024f3b76b70397e1648385528107c5deb16ba7fe29697a570a"} {"question" "q-97426" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{115}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home